Extension API: which colony the colony screen and the build popup show ("COLS").

STATUS: NOT APPLIED — written by work order 180 (B3), parked for Data
(doc/briefs/180-parked-for-data.md, item 1.1). No engine patch may be
applied in that order.

PROOF (work order 180, 27 September 2026): this file is one step of a
series of six (open fixes 35-40, applied in that order on top of
orionlayer-local 9ab84230 — each appends its block after the previous
one). In a scratch clone of the engine, never on orionlayer-local:
`patch -p1 --dry-run` then `patch -p1` applied it cleanly on the steps
before it, and the patched src/ext/ext_api.cpp compiled with the engine's
own flags from out/build/Linux/linux-debug/build.ninja (the ORION2RE_EXT
and debug defines, every include directory, the cmake_pch.hxx include,
-fsyntax-only) — with a control: the same file with `SCREEN_QUEUE_POPUP` misspelt `SCREEN_QUEUE_POPPU` was
refused. A full build of the whole series ran in scratch, only to record
the wire format for OrionLayer's fixtures.

To apply, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, after nothing (it is the first of the series):

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_colony_screen_colony.patch

then rebuild. It comes back off with `patch -R -p1` and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    COLONY::Colony_Screen_ (colony_main.cpp:249-255) and
    COLBLDG::Build_Queue_Popup_ (colbldg.cpp:462-469) take their colony
    from MOX::_screen_data (the star) and COLONY::_orbit_temp, into
    COLONY::_colony_handle. None of the three is in the snapshot, and the
    game opens screen 1 from eight places, several of them its own
    (reports, info, turn summary, colony landing — reading §1), so a
    client cannot know which colony it is looking at. Every value on both
    screens belongs to that one colony.

    THE PAIR AND THE HANDLE ARE BOTH SENT, and a client uses the colony
    only when they agree: the pair is set by every caller BEFORE the
    switch, the handle only by the screen itself, so the first tick at
    the new id (Screen_Control_ ticks before it dispatches, mox2.cpp:40-41)
    carries the previous colony's handle. With the screen's own modes,
    which no field shows: _drawing_display (0 the screen, 2 a planet
    description), COLONY::_field_mode, and autobuild_settings.enabled,
    which decides the autobuild label and what [18] does
    (colony_main.cpp:961-974, :1079-1094).

WIRE, after INFS's place, only while screen 1 or 25 is up:

    "COLS"  int16 _screen_data, int16 _orbit_temp, int16 _colony_handle,
            uint8 _drawing_display, uint8 COLONY::_field_mode,
            uint8 autobuild_settings.enabled

WHAT IT COSTS US WITHOUT IT: the whole colony screen and the whole build
popup stay the game's own picture in OrionLayer's window (the safety
net). HD does not guess the colony.

